The '''2022–23 South African Premiership''' (known as the '''[[South African Premiership|DSTV Premiership]]''' for sponsorship reasons) was the 27th season of the Premier Soccer League since its establishment in [[1996–97 Premier Soccer League|1996]]. It was played from 5 August 2022 to 20 May 2023 <ref>{{Cite web |date=2022-07-06 |title=Premier Soccer League Confirm Start Dates For 2022/2023 Season |url=https://www.soccerladuma.co.za/news/articles/local/categories/south-africa/premier-soccer-league-confirm-start-dates-for-2022-2023-season/720144 |access-date=2022-08-01 |website=Soccer Laduma}}</ref> [[Mamelodi Sundowns F.C.|Mamelodi Sundowns]] successfully defended the title for the 6th time, having won the title from the [[2017–18 South African Premier Division|2017–18]] season.<ref>{{Cite web |title=Premier Soccer League - www.psl.co.za - official website |url=https://psl.co.za/ |access-date=2022-08-01 |website=psl.co.za}}</ref> [[Sekhukhune United F.C.|Sekhukhune United]] relocated from Ellis Park Stadium to Peter Mokaba Stadium.<ref>{{cite web|title=CLUB ANNOUNCEMENT – Official Relocation Of Sekhukhune United FC To Limpopo Province|date=1 July 2022 |url=https://sekhukhuneunitedfc.co.za/club-announcement-official-relocation-of-sekhukhune-united-fc-to-limpopo-province/ |publisher=Sekhukhune United|access-date=1 July 2022}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|title=Sekhukhune relocates from Gauteng to a different province|date=1 July 2022 |url=https://farpost.co.za/latest-news/sekhukhune-relocates-from-gauteng-to-a-province/ |publisher=FARPost|access-date=1 July 2022}}</ref>

